                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "13\\text{ mm}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$13\\text{ mm}$ is the outlier because it is much smaller than the other measurements, which are between $110\\text{ mm}$ and $112\\text{ mm}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 9
      },
      {
        "id": "p74-q7c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p74-q7c-calculation-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 0,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Ignore the outlier and calculate the mean, median and mode of the remaining 5 measurements.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p74-q7c-reason-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Should the outlier be included in reporting the mean, median and mode for this data? ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "break"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Why or why not?",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p74-q7c-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mean: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{557}{5}=111.4\\text{ mm}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; median: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "112\\text{ mm}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; mode: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "112\\text{ mm}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". The mean rises by ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "16.4\\text{ mm}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", the median rises by ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "0.5\\text{ mm}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", and the mode is unchanged. Check the ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "13\\text{ mm}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " record or remeasure the rod; exclude or correct it only if an error is confirmed.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Without $13\\text{ mm}$, the ordered measurements are $110,\\;111,\\;112,\\;112,\\;112\\text{ mm}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Mean}&=\\frac{110+111+112+112+112}{5}\\text{ mm}\\\\\\text{Mean}&=\\frac{557}{5}\\text{ mm}\\\\\\text{Mean}&=111.4\\text{ mm}\\end{align*}$$\nThe median is the third measurement, $112\\text{ mm}$. The mode is also $112\\text{ mm}$, which occurs three times.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Increase in mean}&=(111.4-95)\\text{ mm}\\\\\\text{Increase in mean}&=16.4\\text{ mm}\\\\\\text{Increase in median}&=(112-111.5)\\text{ mm}\\\\\\text{Increase in median}&=0.5\\text{ mm}\\end{align*}$$\nThe mode is unchanged. The mean is affected most.\nThe $13\\text{ mm}$ result is strongly inconsistent with the other measurements of the same rod, but this alone does not prove an error. Check the original record or remeasure the rod. Exclude or correct the result only if a measurement or recording error is confirmed; otherwise retain it.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
